# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository, whatever the checkout platform
# does locally. Godot's own generated .gitattributes carries the same first line;
# a Windows contributor's CRLF would otherwise reach a .gd or .tscn and diff the
# whole file. Measured 2026-09-07: no tracked file carried CRLF, so this changes
# no committed byte.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets go through Git LFS (P5-27, Q124), tracked forward from the
# commit that added these rows: history was not rewritten, the eight files
# tracked then were renormalised into LFS objects in that commit, and every
# binary added since is a pointer in git and an object in LFS. A clone without
# git-lfs installed checks out pointer files; tools/check.sh's import logs
# FreeType failing on the font, and its first FAIL is verify_vehicle's "no node
# in taxi.tscn runs vehicle_lamps.gd" — the body is a pointer, so the mesh
# never instances. That is the message a collaborator sees first.
# `filter=lfs` implies -text; `diff=lfs` and `merge=lfs` keep them undiffed.
*.glb filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ttf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
